WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.060 --> 00:00:06.799
From a gigantic Panda Mei facing off with
Mingzilla, to deleted 4*Town scenes, and a

00:00:06.799 --> 00:00:11.840
rival red panda cousin, the original version
of Pixar's Turning Red was going to be very

00:00:11.840 --> 00:00:12.840
different.

00:00:12.840 --> 00:00:17.160
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, I'm Jan and in
this video I'm revealing the alternate ending

00:00:17.160 --> 00:00:21.949
of Turning Red and the incredible deleted
scenes and storylines you never got to see!

00:00:21.949 --> 00:00:23.920
Spoilers ahead, of course, so take care.

00:00:23.920 --> 00:00:29.849
One of the most spectacular moments in Turning
Red is when Ming's red panda form is finally

00:00:29.849 --> 00:00:30.849
revealed.

00:00:30.849 --> 00:00:31.849
She's huge!

00:00:31.849 --> 00:00:32.849
I told you she was big!

00:00:32.849 --> 00:00:33.970
That big?

00:00:33.970 --> 00:00:39.460
Despite Panda Mei's tiny size in comparison,
she's still able to knock Mingzilla out.

00:00:39.460 --> 00:00:44.600
However, this final face-off was originally
going to be quite different with a giant Red

00:00:44.600 --> 00:00:50.180
Panda Mei going up against her mother in a
Godzilla vs King Kong-style clash.

00:00:50.180 --> 00:00:54.990
In the first draft of the story, Meilin's
red panda grew and shrank in size depending

00:00:54.990 --> 00:00:59.180
on how emotional she got;
and the idea was that, by the very end, Mei

00:00:59.180 --> 00:01:04.110
would get so angry with her mother that she'd
become similarly gigantic.

00:01:04.110 --> 00:01:09.740
What would have led to Mei's massive monster-sized
emotions was, as in the final film, Ming utterly

00:01:09.740 --> 00:01:12.289
humiliating her in front of her beloved boy
band.

00:01:12.289 --> 00:01:13.289
You are in big trouble young lady.

00:01:13.289 --> 00:01:17.280
After already having embarrassed her daughter
in front of her classmates at school and the

00:01:17.280 --> 00:01:19.630
store.

00:01:19.630 --> 00:01:26.649
The two ginormous pandas would have then gone
on to fight in the streets of Toronto in an

00:01:26.649 --> 00:01:28.280
epic kaiju-esque battle.

00:01:28.280 --> 00:01:32.990
The problem, however, was that when the filmmakers
presented their idea, there were lots of questions

00:01:32.990 --> 00:01:38.369
about why Mei would grow to such a size, and
coming up with consistent rules as to how

00:01:38.369 --> 00:01:44.709
or why she'd grow to different sizes at different
times ended up being too complicated and confusing.

00:01:44.709 --> 00:01:49.729
In the end, the filmmakers decided to simplify
Mei's transformation so that she simply poofed

00:01:49.729 --> 00:01:53.749
into a single-sized panda regardless of the
level of her emotions.

00:01:53.749 --> 00:01:59.259
Which perhaps made Ming's transformation into
the absolutely humungous Mingzilla even more

00:01:59.259 --> 00:02:03.289
surprising given we'd only seen Mei's panda
up until that point.

00:02:03.289 --> 00:02:08.140
By the way, The Art of Turning Red book also
has an interesting storyboard of another deleted

00:02:08.140 --> 00:02:12.750
version of the ending where a helicopter news
reporter can be seen reporting on the panda

00:02:12.750 --> 00:02:17.960
showdown in the streets below, followed by
a shot of Mingzilla grabbing Panda Meilin

00:02:17.960 --> 00:02:22.849
and getting ready to spank her, possibly for
the twerking show she put on.

00:02:22.849 --> 00:02:27.640
Also in the book is a version of Mei's panda
where she appears to have what's called "Fire

00:02:27.640 --> 00:02:32.330
Fur", the ability to conjure fire whenever
she's angry, which you can also see in this

00:02:32.330 --> 00:02:37.310
concept art of Meizilla squaring off against
her mother with fiery, red paws.

00:02:37.310 --> 00:02:43.200
A little of this fiery design might have ended
up in the look of Ming's panda with her spiky,

00:02:43.200 --> 00:02:45.610
almost flame-like tail.

00:02:45.610 --> 00:02:49.910
Turning Red director Domee Shi has said there
were eight different versions of the story

00:02:49.910 --> 00:02:52.370
before they settled on the final one.

00:02:52.370 --> 00:02:57.230
And in another early draft, Ming was in fact
pleased about Mei's ability to turn into a

00:02:57.230 --> 00:03:01.299
red panda because "the panda was a good luck
charm for the temple".

00:03:01.299 --> 00:03:05.739
In this version, Ming turned Panda Mei into
a tourist attraction for the shrine that she

00:03:05.739 --> 00:03:10.689
could monetize by having her pose for pictures
and put up with other stuff like being a therapy

00:03:10.689 --> 00:03:12.159
red panda.

00:03:12.159 --> 00:03:17.659
Some aspects of this did end up in the final
film when, after the destruction of the Skydome,

00:03:17.659 --> 00:03:21.400
Panda Mei uses her new-found fame to help
raise funds for its reconstruction.

00:03:21.400 --> 00:03:26.770
And, of course, in the main part of the movie
Mei uses her panda at school to raise money

00:03:26.770 --> 00:03:29.109
for tickets to see 4*Town.

00:03:29.109 --> 00:03:33.659
According to Shi, the first version of the
movie was really "kooky" and a "goofy […] screwball

00:03:33.659 --> 00:03:37.760
kind of comedy" that featured a villain by
the name of Benny Blacktooth.

00:03:37.760 --> 00:03:42.310
Benny was a gangster in Chinatown who was
trying to take over the temple when it started

00:03:42.310 --> 00:03:43.730
running out of money.

00:03:43.730 --> 00:03:48.329
But they later realised the story was getting
far too complicated and veering away from

00:03:48.329 --> 00:03:51.409
its core which was a fantastical tale about
adolescence.

00:03:51.409 --> 00:03:55.640
There's an interesting clip in the Turning
Red trailer which didn't make it into the

00:03:55.640 --> 00:04:00.489
final movie of Meilin and her friends marching
through school with placards, a megaphone,

00:04:00.489 --> 00:04:03.650
and a little drum, protesting environmental
issues.

00:04:03.650 --> 00:04:07.909
Disney's documentary about the making of the
film also has footage of the girls falling

00:04:07.909 --> 00:04:11.930
to the floor as part of the protest with the
other students looking on.

00:04:11.930 --> 00:04:13.301
Power to the people!

00:04:13.301 --> 00:04:18.480
The Art of Turning Red book also has designs
of Mei holding up banners that read "Respect

00:04:18.480 --> 00:04:21.470
Your Mother Earth" and "Hens Should Be Free".

00:04:21.470 --> 00:04:26.760
And there's another deleted scene of Mei watching
TV with Miriam, Priya and Abby and then declaring

00:04:26.760 --> 00:04:29.000
her sudden love for boy band 4*Town.

00:04:29.000 --> 00:04:34.539
I didn't even like 4*Town last year, but now
they're literally the greatest thing that

00:04:34.539 --> 00:04:36.020
ever happened to me!

00:04:36.020 --> 00:04:39.889
Another deleted storyline had Panda Mei officiating
at a wedding.

