00:05:35.240 --> 00:05:39.800
According to the artist, this early concept
art shows a Chinese mafia wedding which I

00:05:39.800 --> 00:05:43.599
think means it was part of the Benny Blacktooth
gangster storyline.

00:05:43.599 --> 00:05:47.979
This makes sense given all the dark-suited
types hanging around the banquet hall.

00:05:47.979 --> 00:05:52.229
It's curious that despite the elaborate setup
there's no guests, and it looks like there

00:05:52.229 --> 00:05:56.699
are some beads of sweat on Mei's forehead,
like she's especially nervous, plus the bride

00:05:56.699 --> 00:05:59.009
does not look happy at all.

00:05:59.009 --> 00:06:03.599
Another intriguing detail is the two merfolk
in tanks on either side of the bride and groom.

00:06:03.599 --> 00:06:09.210
In another iteration of the story, there was
a rivalry and "generational family feud" between

00:06:09.210 --> 00:06:13.979
the Lees and Mei's cousin and aunt who could
both also turn into pandas.

00:06:13.979 --> 00:06:19.550
In that version, Grandma also died and Mei
met her extended family at the funeral.

00:06:19.550 --> 00:06:24.430
That storyline was scrapped because it ended
up becoming too plot-focused and complex,

00:06:24.430 --> 00:06:28.020
rather than centring on the experience of
a young girl growing up.

00:06:28.020 --> 00:06:32.560
Although we did, of course, see Meilin's drawings
of Devon in her notebook, there's several

00:06:32.560 --> 00:06:37.160
other pages we never got to see when Mei ripped
them up after her mum embarrassed her at the

00:06:37.160 --> 00:06:38.229
Daisy Mart.

00:06:38.229 --> 00:06:42.430
Pixar, however, have released the sketches
from the whole notebook online which reveal

00:06:42.430 --> 00:06:47.979
extras pages such as one with Devon as a centaur,
possibly a nod to Onward, and another of Mei

00:06:47.979 --> 00:06:52.990
and her three friends dressed like the protagonists
from the hit anime series Sailor Moon.

00:06:52.990 --> 00:06:57.700
Domee Shi has talked about the influence of
Sailor Moon on Turning Red including "the

00:06:57.700 --> 00:06:59.830
pastels and the dreaminess […] of the nightscapes".

00:06:59.830 --> 00:07:05.009
And some early concept art reveals some more
deleted Sailor Moon easter eggs such this

00:07:05.009 --> 00:07:07.200
one on the wall of Mei's bedroom.

00:07:07.200 --> 00:07:11.289
There's also Luigi and Toad from the Super
Mario franchise in this pic which didn't make

00:07:11.289 --> 00:07:13.020
it into the final movie.

00:07:13.020 --> 00:07:18.659
Another interesting detail in this early concept
art is that Mei's name was originally Fei.

00:07:18.659 --> 00:07:23.039
I've not seen an official explanation given
for the name change, but it's quite possible

00:07:23.039 --> 00:07:27.380
it was altered to avoid repeating the name
of the protagonist, Fei Fei, from Netflix's

00:07:27.380 --> 00:07:30.830
animated feature Over The Moon, which was
released in 2020.

00:07:30.830 --> 00:07:35.530
The title of the movie "Turning Red" has numerous
layers of meaning referring both to Mei's

00:07:35.530 --> 00:07:38.440
literal discovery that she can transform into
a red panda;

00:07:38.440 --> 00:07:42.830
a metaphor also for an adolescent girl getting
her period for the first time.

00:07:42.830 --> 00:07:44.780
Did the red peony bloom?

00:07:44.780 --> 00:07:45.780
No!

00:07:45.780 --> 00:07:46.780
Maybe?

00:07:46.780 --> 00:07:48.659
(GASPS)
And the sense of shame and embarrassment that

00:07:48.659 --> 00:07:53.919
Mei feels whenever her overbearing mother
intervenes in her life outside home, and her

00:07:53.919 --> 00:07:56.319
anger and rebellion against that.

00:07:56.319 --> 00:07:58.669
Plus,
Red is a lucky color.

00:07:58.669 --> 00:08:03.731
However, as revealed in the Disney+ documentary,
there were a lot of different titles also

00:08:03.731 --> 00:08:05.050
considered for the story.

00:08:05.050 --> 00:08:08.629
Many of these were intriguing puns such as
Notorious R.P.G.

00:08:08.629 --> 00:08:14.419
(Red Panda Girl), a play on one of rapper
Biggie Smalls' stage names, The Notorious

00:08:14.419 --> 00:08:17.310
B.I.G.;
My Neighbor Toronto, a reference to Studio

00:08:17.310 --> 00:08:19.860
Ghibli's My Neighbour Totoro;
P.M.S.

00:08:19.860 --> 00:08:25.729
(Panda Mayhem Story), with PMS also standing
for premenstrual syndrome, and Mayhem also

00:08:25.729 --> 00:08:30.659
possibly being a play on Mei's name;
Red and Redder is likely a nod to the movie

00:08:30.659 --> 00:08:34.380
Dumb and Dumber;
Red to Me probably refers to the expression

00:08:34.380 --> 00:08:38.990
"Dead To Me", coincidentally also the title
of an awesome Netflix series;

00:08:38.990 --> 00:08:43.110
and these ones here are another example of
Mei's original name Fei.

00:08:43.110 --> 00:08:48.370
Some other fun deleted scenes in The Art of
Turning Red book include this one of Mei in

00:08:48.370 --> 00:08:54.110
her den under the bed relaxing to music;
Red Panda Mei and friends reading in a store

00:08:54.110 --> 00:08:56.500
or library;
in this scene we see that Mei's favourite

00:08:56.500 --> 00:09:02.170
boy band was called "Boyz In Streets", likely
a mashup of Boyz 2 Men and the Backstreet

00:09:02.170 --> 00:09:04.930
Boys;
there also was a scene of Ming and Mei crying

00:09:04.930 --> 00:09:09.170
while watching a movie or TV show;
and this piece makes me wonder whether Mei

00:09:09.170 --> 00:09:14.620
had a baby sibling in another version;
and then there was an extra A113 easter egg

00:09:14.620 --> 00:09:17.720
in the Skydome stadium that wasn't in the
final film.

00:09:17.720 --> 00:09:22.350
There's even more amazing concept art from
the movie in The Art of Turning Red book,

00:09:22.350 --> 00:09:26.790
so I'll add a link below for where you can
get the book with free shipping worldwide.

00:09:26.790 --> 00:09:31.800
I really loved the finished film, but do you
wish any of these scenes or alternate storylines

00:09:31.800 --> 00:09:32.800
had been included?

